EN = [
"Words scratched on the back with a nail: \"Bren. Seventeen. Told my mother I was twenty.\"",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …So he was seventeen. He told me twenty, too.",
"Skeletons of the Cave",
"…That gate. This is where Bren fell. I was behind that pillar.",
"Look at the floor before the gate. There are hollows worn into it. I didn't see them back then.",
"The crack in the stone under the pillar. There's a scrap of metal wedged in it. …I'll take it out.",
"My leg? It's fine. You don't walk on legs. You walk on stubbornness.",
"We've seen everything before the gate. This time I looked with my eyes open. Go on ahead.",
"Iron Ingot",
"Bram the Smith: See the crest inside the helmet? A single flame and a single sword. That's the Grand Master's own household. A squire or an adjutant would have worn it.",
"Bram the Smith: The words carved under it. 'Guard the gate until your lord returns.' First time I've seen a man engrave his orders into his armor. Afraid he'd forget, I suppose.",
"Bram the Smith: There's a name, too. Hors. Half rusted away. Iron tells no lies. It only rusts.",
"Bram the Smith: Come to think of it, the very first ledger of my family has a line stamped with the same crest. 'Sword of Vice Master Helvar, repair. Payment when his lord returns.' A thousand years on credit.",
"▷ Why didn't his lord come back?",
"Bram the Smith: Ask the iron and it won't know. Ask the archivist. And ask her to collect on that tab while she's at it.",
"Hors, squire to the Grand Master of the Flame Knights\nThe one who kept his back empty until his lord returned",
"A Memory Shown by the Spiral Abyss",
"Someone holding a letter up to the campfire.\n\"…Roran, take this with you. You have to go back north.\"",
"Gold Ingot",
"Bram the Smith: Do you know what it means for a knight to break his own sword? It's taking back a vow. Not to his lord. To the thing he would have to do with that blade.",
"Bram the Smith: And yet he said to mend it. He didn't say throw it away. He meant to take it up again. Once the oath was withdrawn.",
"Bram the Smith: In the ledger there's a drawing where the owner's signature should be. A door. A person standing on the threshold. Helvar. 'He who keeps the threshold,' they called him, and he drew his own nickname with his own hand.",
"▷ What will you do with the sword?",
"Bram the Smith: Take it to its owner, of course. A tab is a tab, and a thing left in my keeping is a thing left in my keeping. If he's somewhere along your road, that is.",
"Underworld Arena",
"The Vice Master's Petition",
"A long text is carved into the wall beside the arena gate. At the top: \"Against the Oath of Three Heads. Vice Master Helvar.\"",
"\"When the rampart is breached, the three captains give up their heads and become a single sentinel. The sentinel erases the name of everything it touches, so the fire has nothing left to eat. It is a weapon to starve the fire to death.\"",
"\"I ask: what is the difference between erasing a name and the fire eating one? We cannot make weapons of our comrades.\"",
"Beneath the text, three lines have been added in other hands. \"Denied. Hargen.\" \"Denied. Isolde.\" \"…I'm sorry. Denied. Merwin.\"",
"Below that, a single line gone over countless times in a thousand years until it is deep: \"Then I will guard the gate. Until my lord returns and withdraws the oath.\"",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …A gate with nothing left behind it to guard. Somebody ought to tell him.",
"Knight Keeping the Oath",
"Soul sand valley. I've never set foot on this ground. Even so, I have to see for myself what's written before that gate.",
"The wall beside the gate. It's a long text. Read from the top line.",
"I've read it. The one man who stood against it. Men like that last the longest. Go on ahead.",
"The Duty Roster on the Wall",
"One whole wall of the arena is covered in gold. Up close, it is writing. Date, watch, anything to report. Hundreds of thousands of lines.",
"The first line: \"Day the oath was sworn. The three captains mounted the plinths. Vice Master Helvar shut the gate and stood. Twenty-four knights who opposed the oath stayed with him.\"",
"As the lines go down, the names of the twenty-four change one by one to 'name forgotten.' Still they stand watch. Written as 'First,' 'Second,' in place of names.",
"The last few hundred years are in a single hand. The same line every day. \"Nothing to report. My lord did not come today either. I stand again tomorrow.\"",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …He kept writing the roster even as he forgot his men's names. Gave them numbers in place of names, if that's what it took. So they wouldn't be left to be forgotten.",
"The Empty Plinths at the Center",
"Three stone plinths stand in the middle of the arena. Nothing rests on them. A head once sat on each.",
"Only the tops of the plinths are worn to a shine. The grain of a cloth wiping them. Every day for a thousand years. Not a speck of ash on the floor around them.",
"Knee marks are worn into the floor before the plinths. Where he knelt each time he wiped them. All three. The place of the oath he opposed was tended most carefully by the man who opposed it.",
"Small letters beneath the third plinth: \"Merwin, you wrote that you were sorry. So am I.\"",
"Beacon Keepers of the Nether",
"Inside the arena. Where someone has lived a long time, their habits stay behind. Start with the wall.",
"That whole wall. I took it for gilding, but it's writing. A duty roster.",
"Three plinths in the middle. The tops are empty. See what used to sit there.",
"A thousand years standing watch alone, is that it. …Twenty was long enough for me.",
"Now I know how he lived. Now we can fight him. Go on out first.",
"Knights Guarding the Place of the Oath",
"Helvar. He who keeps the threshold of the underworld. …The line I left empty that day, I'll fill it in today.",
"Helvar, Vice Master of the Flame Knights\nThe one who refused the oath, and guarded the place of the oath to the very end",
"Bram Closing the Ledger",
"Bram the Smith: (He draws one thick stroke across the line in the ledger.) Sword of Vice Master Helvar. Repair. Paid.",
"Archivist Isabel: (She opens the Chronicle to the empty line.) Vice Master Helvar. The one who said comrades cannot be made into weapons. Who broke his sword, shut the gate, and stood to the end.",
"Archivist Isabel: And the twenty-four. Their names were erased even from the duty roster, but I'll write that they existed. 'Twenty-four knights who opposed the oath and stayed with the Vice Master.'",
"Bram the Smith: That young lady writes down even the ones who were erased. A good habit. Iron's the same. Iron remembers what used to be where the rust is.",
"▷ Why didn't his lord come to withdraw the oath?",
"Archivist Isabel: …He couldn't come, I think. If that knight in the dream is Arden. He is still inside the fire, even now.",
"Helvar. …Stubborn fool.\nI should have told you with my own mouth that you were right.",
"Glow Berries",
"Jungle Temple",
"Kael's Scribbles · One",
"Words cut with a knife into the entrance pillar. The strokes are light and crooked. Written while laughing.",
"\"Roran counts heads twice. I'm the first to make him count three times. — Kael, second in command\"",
"Below it in another hand: \"No scribbling on ruins. — Captain\" And below that, crooked again: \"This is scribbling too.\"",
"Kael's Scribbles · Two",
"The wall of the inner room. The handwriting has changed. The strokes are deep and straight. There are many numbers.",
"\"Two in the cave. One at the gate. One in the forest. One at the cliff. About one every five days.\" A small tick is cut at the end of each line. He is counting.",
"\"The letter says only 'look, and come back.' Why does looking need twelve of us? Why give an ember to every one?\"",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …I've never seen this one. He was keeping count of this?",
"Kael's Scribbles · Three",
"The innermost wall, close to the floor. The height of someone writing while seated. Campfire soot still marks the wall.",
"\"I held the letter up to the fire. There is one more line.\" The half line after it has been scraped away with a knife. The writer erased it himself.",
"\"Roran. I'll tell you the southern sun is calling us. You'll believe it. You go north. Don't go to have it out with them. Because you're the kind who would.\"",
"The last line is very small: \"I'm leaving the ember behind. With that on me, I can be seen.\"",
"This is the temple. Where Kael made camp. He scribbled on every wall. I was angry about it back then.",
"The entrance pillar. That crooked handwriting. He wrote it laughing.",
"There's another on the wall of the inner room. …The handwriting's changed. A lot of numbers.",
"The innermost part, close to the floor. The height of someone sitting down to write. Right by where the campfire was.",
"Watch between the vines. You won't see a foliaath until you're close.",
"Read them all, in order. …He was talking to me. For twenty years. Go on ahead.",
"Drowned Below the Cliff",
"Desert Village",
"The Calendar Stone by the Well",
"The stones around the well are densely scored with marks. Each line a date, a direction, a count of paces. Carved by one generation after another. The top line is so worn it can be read only by fingertip.",
"\"Seventeenth day. Sank below the second hill to the west.\" \"Seventeenth day. Sank three hundred paces east of that.\" The interval never once slips. For three hundred years.",
"Beside the stone, a line added in a child's hand: \"When the guest who calls the water passes, grass comes up three days later. Don't build houses on the guest's road. Don't wake the guest. The guest is working.\"",
"At the very bottom is one new line, cut hastily with a knife. About twenty years old. Crooked letters: \"The next stretch is the middle of the caravan road. Told the village. Told them to move the road. — a passerby\"",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …That's Kael's handwriting. He read this on his way across, worked out where the ground would sink next, warned the village, and went on. On a road he was walking alone, like a hunted man.",
"The desert village. We filled our water here during the expedition, too. The well is over there.",
"The stones around the well. Covered in marks. This is what the old man was talking about.",
"You ask the people who live there about the road. I should have heard them out twenty years ago. Let's go.",
"The Sandworm's Nest",
"Waterway Plans on the Tunnel Wall",
"The tunnel walls are strangely straight. Not a collapsed tunnel but a finished passage. A channel is cut along the wall, and its bed is white with scale. Water once ran here.",
"A stone slab is set into the wall. Lines and gradations. The design for a waterway. Each section bears a mark: one claw scratch for every section dug. Thousands of them.",
"\"By order of Amrat, King of the Desert. The waterway shall be joined to the king's garden. The digging is entrusted to the king's beast, Sirok.\" Sirok, in the old tongue, means 'that which calls the water.'",
"The last section on the plan, 'the king's garden,' has no claw scratch. Everything up to the section before it has been dug. Where the garden stood is under the sand. The beast has been digging for a thousand years toward a last section it can never reach.",
"Husks of the Desert",
"Wall Painting in the Water Store",
"A painting runs across the wall of the lower room in six panels. The first: the king holds a single small worm in both hands. The worm drinks the water in his palm.",
"The second and third panels: the worm grows. The king draws a line in the sand with his staff, and the worm digs along it. Water flows where it has dug. A village appears. Each time a section is done, the king pours it a jar of water.",
"The fourth panel: the sky is ash grey. Seven people stand before a fire, and the king walks toward them. He looks back and beckons to the beast. Beneath it, the words: \"I will wait in the garden. The day the water reaches it, I will open the gate for you. Until then, do not stop your work, Sirok.\"",
"The fifth panel: the king returns carrying an eye. But the kingdom in the painting is half sunk in sand. The price of receiving the eye. The king goes in through the garden gate, and sand closes over the gate.",
"The sixth panel was painted much later by another hand. It is clumsy. The beast digs alone. Beside it, small people carrying water jars. The villagers. For generations they poured the water in the king's place.",
"Water Bucket",
"Sirok the Sandworm",
"Husks of the Sunken Road",
"Sirok, that which calls the water\nCarried out for a thousand years the order to join the waterway to the king's garden. Work complete.",
"Cooked Mutton",
"Sweet Berries",
"Roran by the Campfire",
"Expedition Captain Roran: Thomas couldn't whistle. All that came out was wind. When Lia imitated it, the whole camp laughed.",
"Expedition Captain Roran: Bren never took his boots off to sleep. So he could run at any moment. The youngest was the most afraid, and the first to stand in front.",
"Expedition Captain Roran: Marco and Danilo are brothers. Marco had a good sense of direction and Danilo the opposite. So Danilo always walked behind his little brother.",
"Expedition Captain Roran: Ines had no fear. No, she had it, she just never showed it. Jonah never said a word, and Fei did the talking for both of them.",
"Expedition Captain Roran: Hayun liked high places. Otto could sing. When Hayun climbed, Otto would sing to her from below. So she wouldn't lose the way back down.",
"Archivist Isabel: And Kael?",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …Every time I counted heads, Kael hid one person behind him. To watch me panic. That's how I got the habit of counting twice. It's his fault.",
"Igloo of the Snowfield",
"Scribbles Sealed in the Ice",
"Something shows beneath the ice floor where the giant lies. It was drawn on the floor before it froze. Clumsy lines. A children's drawing.",
"One big white beast with several small people riding on its back. The beast is drawn with a smiling face. Beside it, crooked letters: \"Our bear. Haven't decided on a name yet.\"",
"Something has been added to one side of the drawing in a different color. The children hold a glowing stone out to the beast. The letters are hurried: \"They say the king is turning to ice. They say we'll freeze too. This is a cold stone. If the fire comes, put it out with this. You keep it. We'll be right back.\"",
"The giant sleeps face down upon that drawing. A faint blue light leaks from within its arms. In a thousand years it has not once shifted. For fear the drawing would be rubbed away.",
"The Hunters' Wall",
"The inner wall of the igloo is layered with writing in charcoal. A different hunter wrote each winter.",
"\"Buried Jorn in the snow. Went the next day and he was gone. Not dug up. The snow was swept aside to left and right. Footprints twice the height of a man.\"",
"\"Corpse thief. A white thing. Big as three bears. Takes only the dead. Doesn't touch the game. Leaves our food alone too.\"",
"\"Tracked it to the mouth of its den. Jorn was standing there. Frozen. Upright. Under an overhang so the snow wouldn't cover him. Went there angry and couldn't be angry.\"",
"The newest writing, in a shaking hand: \"Broke my leg in the blizzard. Thought I was done for. The white thing came and sniffed at me. A long time. Then it put me on its back. Woke up at the igloo door. Seems it doesn't take the ones still alive.\"",
"Expedition Captain Roran: …Danilo, Jonah, Fei. I never found where they lay. I thought it was because the snow had covered them. If someone carried them off before it could.",
"The hunters' igloo. A different one stays here every winter. Look at the wall.",
"The inner wall. Charcoal writing, layer on layer. This time we read to the end.",
"So it wasn't wolves. Let's go. The cave deep in the snowfield.",
]
